## Add the Knowledge Graph SPARQL playground

Context: Add a read-only SPARQL workspace beside GraphQL on the Knowledge
Graph Query page. Users can run SELECT queries, inspect generated SQL, export
results, and explicitly send triple-shaped rows to Explorer without Run
navigating away.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/QuerySafety.py
   Centralize the read-only SPARQL mutation gate.
2. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Enforce the gate on execute and translate routes.
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/tools.py
   Reuse the shared SPARQL safety rule.
4. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_query.html
   Add the shared GraphQL/SPARQL Query shell.
5. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_graphql.html
   Preserve GraphiQL as the GraphQL tab pane.
6. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sparql.html
   Add the SPARQL editor and result workspace.
7. src/front/static/query/js/query-execute.js
   Run samples and render results, SQL, CSV, and Explorer actions.
8. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   Load triple-shaped query results into Explorer.
9. src/front/static/query/css/query-sparql.css
   Add token-based responsive split layout.
10. src/front/static/global/css/query.css
    Retarget existing Grid.js styling to the SPARQL results pane.
11. tests/
    Cover the safety boundary, Query markup, controller behavior, and deep link.
12. README.md, docs/user-guide.md, docs/data-access.md, and docs/sphinx/api/app.core.w3c.rst
    Document the playground, execution path, and an executable triple-query example.

